  "raw": {
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205016556484_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct-Emergency Management (Subject Matter Experts)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nAlvernia University Subject Matter Experts and Adjunct Faculty – Emergency Management College of Health Sciences  Position Type : Part-Time / Adjunct / Course Development Opportunities  Location : Alvernia University, Reading, Pennsylvania (Online Instruction) Position Summary Alvernia University invites applications from qualified professionals and educators to serve as Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) and Adjunct Faculty in support of its developing Emergency Management academic programs. We are seeking individuals with advanced academic preparation, professional expertise, and a passion for educating the next generation of emergency management professionals. Opportunities include curriculum and course development, online instruction, and the integration of contemporary industry practices into academic coursework. Successful candidates will contribute to the development and delivery of innovative, career-relevant courses that prepare students to address complex challenges in emergency preparedness, disaster response, community resilience, public safety, and emergency management leadership. Areas of Expertise Alvernia University is particularly interested in candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: · Public Health and Emergency Preparedness : Public health emergencies, pandemic preparedness, community health resilience, and interagency coordination. ·  Emergency Operations and Planning : Emergency operations plans, incident command systems, continuity of operations, crisis management, and multiagency coordination. · GIS and Data Analytics for Emergency Management : Geographic information systems, spatial analysis, data visualization, predictive modeling, and technology-supported emergency decision-making. · Risk, Hazard, and Vulnerability Assessment : Hazard identification, risk analysis, vulnerability assessment, mitigation strategies, and community resilience planning. · Disaster Response and Recovery : Disaster operations, resource coordination, recovery planning, disaster assistance, and long-term community recovery. · Public Administration and Emergency Management Leadership : Public policy, government operations, intergovernmental relations, organizational leadership, budgeting, and emergency management administration. Primary Responsibilities Depending on qualifications and institutional needs, selected candidates may participate in course development, instruction, or both. Course Development · Collaborate with academic leadership and instructional design professionals to develop engaging, high-quality online courses. · Develop course objectives, instructional materials, assignments, assessments, and applied learning activities aligned with program outcomes. · Integrate current industry standards, emerging technologies, professional practices, and real-world case studies. · Ensure course content reflects contemporary emergency management challenges and workforce expectations. Adjunct Teaching · Deliver engaging and academically rigorous instruction in an online learning environment. · Facilitate student learning through discussion, applied projects, case studies, and practical exercises. · Assess student performance and provide timely, constructive feedback. · Support student success while maintaining high academic and professional standards. · Collaborate with program leadership to ensure curriculum relevance and continuous improvement. Required Qualifications · Master's degree or higher from an accredited institution in Emergency Management, Public Health, Public Administration, Homeland Security, Disaster Science, Geographic Information Systems, or a closely related discipline. · Demonstrated professional or academic expertise in at least one of the identified subject areas. · Strong written and verbal communication skills. · Ability to translate complex disciplinary concepts into meaningful and accessible learning experiences. · Commitment to academic excellence, student success, and Alvernia University's Franciscan values. Preferred Qualifications · Previous experience teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level, particularly in online or asynchronous environments. · Experience developing online courses or academic curricula. · Professional experience with emergency management agencies, public health organizations, government entities, healthcare systems, or related industries. · Relevant certifications or specialized training, including FEMA, Incident Command System (ICS), GIS, or other emergency management credentials. · Experience collaborating across disciplines and applying emerging technologies to emergency management practice. Application Process Interested candidates should submit: · A current curriculum vitae or résumé. · A letter of interest identifying specific areas of expertise and interest in course development, adjunct teaching, or both. · A brief description of relevant professional, teaching, or curriculum development experience. Applications will be reviewed as opportunities become available. About Alvernia University Alvernia University is a Franciscan institution committed to academic excellence, ethical leadership, service, and the preparation of graduates who make meaningful contributions to their professions and communities. Through innovative academic programming and strong connections to professional practice, the University prepares students to respond to evolving workforce needs and serve the greater good. Alvernia University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from qualified candidates with diverse professional and educational experiences.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204976812025_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Regional Site Manager - Pottsville, PA",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nJob Summary: The O’Pake Institute for Economic Development & Entrepreneurship is seeking a Regional Site Manager who will report to the Assistant Director of Student Experiential Learning. The Regional Site Manager will have responsibilities including supporting the O’Pake Institute’s EmpowerED program and Fellows Program which includes students from high school through advanced degree programs. This position will focus on overseeing student-powered internal partnership and client services projects, requiring strong project management skills, along with excellent written and verbal communication, are essential.  Essential Functions:  Promote Franciscan ideals and adherence to the Mission of the University as demonstrated by the University's Ideal Characteristics. As we are an equal opportunity employer committed to Franciscan values, all employees share responsibility for advancing belonging of others in the performance of their roles while demonstrating service orientation, respect for all, intellectual curiosity, solution focus and innovation, and mutual accountability.   Management of Client Services Projects:  Manage a team of students, providing mentorship and technical expertise as they contribute to the development, execution, and delivery of defined outcomes for O’Pake clients, while fostering experiential learning opportunities that enhance their professional growth and hands-on skills. In addition, manage the relationship and associated projects with identified clients. In conjunction with O’Pake home office Staff, coordinate intern team transition semesterly and schedules to ensure consistent engagement.  In partnership with the O’Pake Client Services team, manage client-facing projects involving students, such as Community and Economic Development, Innovation and Tech-Transfer, Creative Services, Business and Strategic Planning and Financial Services, and Venture Investment Services.  Create an environment of continuous learning, where students gain real-world experience and enhance their professional skills in a dynamic, client-focused setting.  Support the development of O’Pake Fellows and EmpowerED High School Students in developing their experiential learning skills and professional development.  Program Coordination: EmpowerED & O’Pake Fellows Programs  This role supports the full student lifecycle, from recruitment through engagement and retention, for both the EmpowerED High School Internship Program and the O’Pake Fellows Program, ensuring students experience meaningful, skills-based hands-on learning aligned with the mission of the Institute.   Recruitment & Outreach Support recruitment efforts for both EmpowerED high school interns and O’Pake Fellows, including outreach, application management, and participation in recruitment events.  Develop and maintain relationships in close collaboration with the O’Pake Institute, partnering with school districts, regional organizations, and community stakeholders to strengthen engagement and expand impact.  Assist in developing strategies and execution to convert at least 20% of EmpowerED high school interns into O’Pake Fellows.  Retention, Engagement & Student Support  Provide day-to-day oversight, coaching, and support to EmpowerED high school interns, ensuring they have the tools, curriculum, and guidance needed to apply classroom learning to hands-on project work.  Track student progress, manage onboarding processes, and monitor engagement milestones for both programs.  Coordinate experiential learning opportunities that enhance student development and promote long-term program involvement.  Campus & Community Collaboration  Partner with the Office of Career Development and Student Admissions and Enrollment, and other university stakeholders, to create integrated experiential learning pathways.  Build collaborative relationships with community organizations and industry partners to support meaningful applied-learning experiences.  Program Quality & Continuous Improvement  Assist with program reviews, needs assessments, and enhancement initiatives for both the EmpowerED and Fellows Programs. Administrative & Operational Support  Maintain accurate records, documentation, and program data. Assist with planning and executing orientations, trainings, workshops, and student engagement events.  Internal Partnership Management  Participate with O’Pake Staff and stakeholders in representing O’Pake in all identified external stakeholder facing events and opportunities, specifically those their dedicated regional territory.  Support other internal partnerships contributing to O’Pake’s university integration.  Other duties as assigned.  Qualifications/Education  A bachelor's degree in education, marketing, or a related field is required; a master’s degree is preferred.  Expertise in general business knowledge and education.  Proven experience in managing K-12 students, career readiness, and student programming.  Strong management, organizational, and project management skills, with exceptional attention to detail.  Proficiency in MS Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint),  Ability to work independently, proactively multitask, and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment.  Flexibility in work hours and some travel required for K-12 institution visits, career fairs, and related activities.  Physical Requirements: In person attendance is required in order to perform the duties of this job. Time expected = 20 hours/week.  Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer.  Must be able to lift 15 pounds at times.",
      "department": ""
    },
