e an environment of continuous learning, where students gain real-world experience and enhance their professional skills in a dynamic, client-focused setting.  Support the development of O’Pake Fellows and EmpowerED High School Students in developing their experiential learning skills and professional development.  Program Coordination: EmpowerED & O’Pake Fellows Programs  This role supports the full student lifecycle, from recruitment through engagement and retention, for both the EmpowerED High School Internship Program and the O’Pake Fellows Program, ensuring students experience meaningful, skills-based hands-on learning aligned with the mission of the Institute.   Recruitment & Outreach Support recruitment efforts for both EmpowerED high school interns and O’Pake Fellows, including outreach, application management, and participation in recruitment events.  Develop and maintain relationships in close collaboration with the O’Pake Institute, partnering with school districts, regional organizations, and community stakeholders to strengthen engagement and expand impact.  Assist in developing strategies and execution to convert at least 20% of EmpowerED high school interns into O’Pake Fellows.  Retention, Engagement & Student Support  Provide day-to-day oversight, coaching, and support to EmpowerED high school interns, ensuring they have the tools, curriculum, and guidance needed to apply classroom learning to hands-on project work.  Track student progress, manage onboarding processes, and monitor engagement milestones for both programs.  Coordinate experiential learning opportunities that enhance student development and promote long-term program involvement.  Campus & Community Collaboration  Partner with the Office of Career Development and Student Admissions and Enrollment, and other university stakeholders, to create integrated experiential learning pathways.  Build collaborative relationships with community organizations and industry partners to support meaningful applied-learning experiences.  Program Quality & Continuous Improvement  Assist with program reviews, needs assessments, and enhancement initiatives for both the EmpowerED and Fellows Programs. Administrative & Operational Support  Maintain accurate records, documentation, and program data. Assist with planning and executing orientations, trainings, workshops, and student engagement events.  Internal Partnership Management  Participate with O’Pake Staff and stakeholders in representing O’Pake in all identified external stakeholder facing events and opportunities, specifically those their dedicated regional territory.  Support other internal partnerships contributing to O’Pake’s university integration.  Other duties as assigned.  Qualifications/Education  A bachelor's degree in education, marketing, or a related field is required; a master’s degree is preferred.  Expertise in general business knowledge and education.  Proven experience in managing K-12 students, career readiness, and student programming.  Strong management, organizational, and project management skills, with exceptional attention to detail.  Proficiency in MS Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint),  Ability to work independently, proactively multitask, and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment.  Flexibility in work hours and some travel required for K-12 institution visits, career fairs, and related activities.  Physical Requirements: In person attendance is required in order to perform the duties of this job. Time expected = 20 hours/week.  Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer.  Must be able to lift 15 pounds at times.",
