    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204780323011_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Forensic Science, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nAlvernia University’s College of Innovation, Discovery, and Enterprise invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor of Forensic Science to begin in the Fall 2027 semester. The successful candidate will contribute expertise in one or more areas of forensic science, such as forensic toxicology, forensic chemistry, forensic biology, criminalistics, or another area of forensic science through undergraduate teaching, curriculum development, scholarly activity, and student mentoring. The successful candidate will play a significant role in the continued development of the University’s Forensic Science program and its pursuit of FEPAC accreditation, with the potential to assume a leadership role, including serving as Program Director. Required Qualifications: Candidates must meet one of the following qualifications: Hold a minimum of a master’s degree (or equivalent) in forensic science or in a discipline appropriate to a forensic science area offered by the program, along with a minimum of five years of full-time (or equivalent) relevant professional experience in forensic science; OR   Hold a doctorate in forensic science or a discipline appropriate to a forensic science area offered by the program. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience at the undergraduate level; Experience working in a forensic science laboratory or other professional forensic science setting; Experience developing forensic science curricula or programs; Evidence of scholarly activity or potential for scholarly activity in the candidate’s area of expertise; Leadership and/or program accreditation experience. How to Apply: Candidates should submit: Cover letter Current curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy  Research/scholarly activity statement  Three letters of recommendation Official transcripts Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  Alvernia University is an equal opportunity employer. Employees are expected to promote Franciscan ideals and advance the University’s mission through a commitment to service, respect for all, intellectual curiosity, innovation, and mutual accountability. All members of the community share responsibility for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion. At this time, Alvernia University is unable to sponsor employment-based work visas for applicants . Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship from the University. About Alvernia University  Alvernia University is a Franciscan Catholic institution located in Reading, Pennsylvania, founded in 1958 by the Bernardine Franciscan Sisters. The university serves approximately 3,000 students across its main campus, branch campuses, and online programs. Alvernia offers a distinctive blend of a rigorous liberal arts education, strong professional preparation, experiential learning opportunities, and a deep commitment to community engagement rooted in Franciscan values. The University has been recognized as a Best National University by U.S. News & World Report (2024), a College of Distinction, and one of Money Magazine’s Best Colleges (2024). Employee Benefits: Join a team that values your well-being! We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support you and your family: Robust Health Coverage:  Choose from three offered medical plans, plus dental and vision. Financial Security:  Enjoy University-paid life/AD&D insurance and long-term disability, with options for short-term disability and supplemental coverage for you and your family (including accident, critical illness, and hospital indemnity plans). Flexible spending accounts are also available. Exceptional Retirement:  Start saving immediately with our 403(b) Retirement Plan . You'll get 100% immediate vesting , a University gift contribution, and a generous match up to 5% of your deferrals. Time Off:  Take advantage of 20  paid holidays each year, including 5 floating holidays. Invest in Your Future:  Enjoy tuition remission benefits for yourself and your dependents. On-Campus Wellness:  Benefit-eligible employees on our main campus receive free access to our Medical & Counseling Center. Employee Meal Plan : This plan provides convenient, flexible dining options on campus at a reduced cost.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204780237038_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct- Assistant Women's Bowling Coach (Part-time)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nJob Posting Title Assistant Bowling Coach (Part-Time) Job Description Position:   Assistant Bowling Coach (Part-Time)   Essential Functions: In compliance with policies, procedures, and regulations of Alvernia University, the NCAA, and the MAC, directs and organizes all aspects and job responsibilities of an assistant coach as indicated in the Alvernia University Coaches Manual. Responsible for assisting the University's intercollegiate athletics program and establishing policies and procedures that achieve the parallel goals of development of quality, competitive athletics teams and support of the individual educational goals of student-athletes. Assist in the recruitment and retention of academically and athletically qualified student-athletes. Represent and/or carry out the duties of the head coach in his/her absence.  Maintain an active understanding of all University, NCAA and MAC rules and regulations and report any possible violation immediately to the Director of Athletics. Pass the NCAA Division III Recruiting Test. Promote Franciscan ideals and adherence to the Mission of the University.   Additional Responsibilities: Attend all mandatory meetings, training sessions, etc. Contribute to the overall success of the intercollegiate athletics program by performing all other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Head Coach and/or Director of Athletics   Position Requirements: Bachelor’s degree. Prior coaching and/or playing experience (preferably at the collegiate level). Knowledge of NCAA Division III rules. CPR Certification required. Commitment to the mission, core values, and goals of Alvernia University Ability to work nights and weekends.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204780327152_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Physician Associate Principal Faculty Member",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPosition Summary  This is a full-time, in-person, non-tenure track faculty position in the emerging Physician Associate (PA) Program, which is housed in the College of Health Sciences (CHS) at Alvernia University. Faculty will report directly to the PA Program Director. This principal faculty position is instrumental in the day-to-day operations of the Physician Associate Program and the education of its students. The program location will be at the John R. Post Center, Reading CollegeTowne site. Additional compensation may be available for administrative responsibilities assigned by the Program Director and performed beyond standard faculty duties, in accordance with institutional guidelines and subject to appropriate approval. Principal Faculty Duties and Responsibilities  Develop, evaluate, revise, and coordinate didactic and clinical year curriculum Work in collaboration with the Program Director and instructional faculty produce and deliver curriculum content Instruct didactic and clinical year students Develop and evaluate didactic and clinical year student assessments Mentor and advise physician assistant students Participate in the development and any necessary revision of the PA Program Mission Statement, Goals, and competencies Participate in the evaluation of the overall effectiveness of the Program in meeting its mission and goals Select applicants for admissions to the PA Program Provide academic counseling Participate in student remediation Participate in programmatic self-assessment and planning Evaluate student performance Provide instruction of content related to clinical expertise and as assigned by course directors Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong organizational skills and keen attention to detail Adept interpersonal and communication skills Skillful problem-solving capabilities An ability to work effectively in a team environment Personal accountability for all duties outlined in the job description and as assigned by the Program Director Supervision  Received : PA Program Director  Given : N/A Minimum Qualifications NCCPA certification At least three years of clinical experience as a physician assistant Master’s Degree or higher  Employee Benefits: Join a team that values your well-being! We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support you and your family: Robust Health Coverage:  Choose from three offered medical plans, plus dental and vision. Financial Security:  Enjoy University-paid life/AD&D insurance and long-term disability, with options for short-term disability and supplemental coverage for you and your family (including accident, critical illness, and hospital indemnity plans). Flexible spending accounts are also available. Exceptional Retirement:  Start saving immediately with our 403(b) Retirement Plan . You will get 100% immediate vesting , a University gift contribution, and a generous match up to 5% of your deferrals. Time Off:  Take advantage of 18 paid holidays each year. Invest in Your Future:  Enjoy tuition remission benefits for yourself and your dependents. On-Campus Wellness:  Benefit-eligible employees on our main campus receive free access to our Medical & Counseling Center. Employee Meal Plan : This plan provides convenient, flexible dining options on campus at a reduced cost.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204779281835_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Criminal Justice, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nAssistant or Associate Professor of Criminal Justice, Tenure Track The Criminal Justice Department at Alvernia University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position beginning either Spring 2027 or Fall 2027, as negotiated. The position is housed within the College of Humanities, Education, and Social Sciences. Criminal Justice is one of the university’s longest-standing programs and is supported by strong complementary disciplines, including social work, addictions and mental health treatment, psychology, forensic science, political science, and cybersecurity. The department benefits from robust partnerships with local agencies and a dedicated crime investigation house that supports interprofessional, hands-on simulations. Alvernia prepares both residential undergraduate students and adult learners for a wide range of careers through a strong foundation in theory paired with experiential learning opportunities that develop practical and professional skills. The successful candidate will demonstrate excellence in teaching, strong communication and interpersonal skills, and a record of scholarly engagement appropriate to experience. This position is primarily focused on in-person instruction within the university’s traditional undergraduate program, with an emphasis on active student engagement and presence on campus. Preferred Qualifications and Areas of Interest  The College particularly welcomes candidates with: Ability to teach courses such as writing for criminal justice professionals, research methods, corrections, probation and parole, and law enforcement-related courses A commitment to developing student-centered programming and experiential learning opportunities Interest in fostering partnerships with community agencies and organizations A demonstrated commitment to mission, diversity, equity, and inclusion Responsibilities  The standard teaching load is 4/4. The successful candidate will: Teach in-person undergraduate courses across the curriculum, from introductory to capstone levels Potentially teach a section of the First-Year Search Seminar in the fall semester, as a part of the contractual load Actively contribute to the life of the department through student advising, mentorship, and engagement in co-curricular and extracurricular activities, including career exploration events and partnerships with local agencies Support the department’s strong emphasis on service, community engagement, and student development Engage in ongoing scholarly activities and develop or continue a research agenda appropriate to the discipline and the candidate’s professional interests Eligibility Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Criminal Justice or a closely related field or provide evidence that the degree will be completed by August 15, 2027. Alvernia University is an equal opportunity employer. Employees are expected to promote Franciscan ideals and advance the University’s mission through a commitment to service, respect for all, intellectual curiosity, innovation, and mutual accountability. All members of the community share responsibility for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion. Applications received by October 20, 2026, will receive full consideration. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check. Employee Benefits: Join a team that values your well-being! We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support you and your family: Robust Health Coverage: Choose from three offered medical plans, plus dental and vision. Financial Security: Enjoy University-paid life/AD&D insurance and long-term disability, with options for short-term disability and supplemental coverage for you and your family (including accident, critical illness, and hospital indemnity plans). Flexible spending accounts are also available. Exceptional Retirement: Start saving immediately with our 403(b) Retirement Plan . You'll get 100% immediate vesting , a University gift contribution, and a generous match up to 5% of your deferrals. Time Off: Take advantage of 20 paid holidays each year, including 5 floating holidays. Invest in Your Future: Enjoy tuition remission benefits for yourself and your dependents. On-Campus Wellness: Benefit-eligible employees on our main campus receive free access to our Medical & Counseling Center. Employee Meal Plan : This plan provides convenient, flexible dining options on campus at a reduced cost.",
