      "title": "Part-Time MBA Adjunct - Reading and Allentown locations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nExperienced professionals with an MBA or significant relevant industry experience are encouraged to apply and contribute to our accredited MBA program through both online and in-person instruction. Preference will be given to doctorally qualified candidates to support the program's accreditation standards. As our MBA program continues to expand, including the recent launch of a hybrid MBA program in Allentown, we are also seeking professionals who are interested in teaching part-time, in-person, at our Allentown location.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204554878099_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct-Gross Anatomy Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-29\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPhysician Associate Program  College of Health Sciences  Alvernia University Alvernia University invites applications for an Adjunct Faculty position to teach Gross Anatomy in the systems-based curriculum in the Master of Medical Science Physician Associate (PA) Program within the College of Health Sciences. The successful candidate will provide high-quality instruction in graduate-level human gross anatomy, integrating foundational anatomical knowledge with clinical application to prepare physician associate students for didactic and clinical education. Instruction includes classroom and laboratory teaching utilizing advanced anatomy visualization technology, including the Anatomage Table, while fostering an engaging, collaborative, and student-centered learning environment. Essential Responsibilities · Teach Gross Anatomy within the Physician Associate Program in accordance with the approved curriculum and course learning outcomes. · Deliver high-quality instruction through lectures, laboratory experiences, and active learning strategies. · Facilitate learning through the use of advanced anatomy visualization technology. · Develop and administer assessments that measure student achievement of course objectives. · Provide timely feedback and academic support to students. · Maintain accurate course records and submit grades in accordance with University policies. · Collaborate with program faculty to ensure curricular integration and continuous quality improvement. · Participate in course evaluation and revision as needed to support program effectiveness and accreditation standards. · Maintain compliance with University policies and applicable accreditation requirements. Required Qualifications · Master's degree or higher in Anatomy, Anatomical Sciences, Medicine, Physician Associate Studies, Physical Therapy, Occupational Therapy, or a closely related health sciences discipline. · Experience teaching gross anatomy at the graduate and/or professional level is required. · Demonstrated expertise in human anatomy and its clinical application. · Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. · Commitment to excellence in teaching and student success. Preferred Qualifications · Terminal degree (PhD, MD, DO, DMSc, DSc, EdD, or equivalent) in a related discipline. · Experience teaching in a Physician Associate, medical, or other graduate health professions program. · Experience with advanced anatomy visualization technology and laboratory instruction. · Familiarity with instructional technologies and active learning methodologies. About Alvernia University Alvernia University is a comprehensive Catholic university rooted in the Franciscan tradition, committed to academic excellence, ethical leadership, and service to others. The Physician Associate Program prepares compassionate, competent, and collaborative healthcare professionals through innovative education, experiential learning, and community engagement. Alvernia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from individuals committed to fostering excellence and belonging in higher education.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204554867898_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct- Medical Physiology Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-29\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPhysician Associate Program  College of Health Sciences  Alvernia University Alvernia University invites applications for an Adjunct Faculty position to teach Medical Physiology within the Master of Medical Science Physician Associate (PA) Program in the College of Health Sciences. The successful candidate will provide high-quality instruction in graduate-level medical physiology, emphasizing the integration of physiological principles with clinical application to support physician associate student development. The course content will focus on the normal function of human body systems and the application of physiological concepts to understanding disease processes, clinical assessment, and patient care. The instructor will foster an engaging, collaborative, and student-centered learning environment that supports student success within the PA curriculum. Essential Responsibilities · Teach Medical Physiology within the Physician Associate Program in accordance with approved curriculum objectives and course learning outcomes. · Deliver graduate-level instruction through evidence-based teaching strategies, including lectures, case-based learning, active learning activities, and other instructional methodologies. · Integrate foundational physiology concepts with clinical applications relevant to physician associate practice. · Develop, administer, and evaluate assessments that measure student achievement of course objectives and learning outcomes. · Provide timely feedback and academic support to students. · Maintain accurate course records, including attendance and grades, in accordance with University policies. · Collaborate with PA Program faculty to ensure curricular integration, appropriate sequencing of content, and continuous quality improvement. · Participate in course evaluation and revision processes as needed. · Maintain compliance with University policies and applicable accreditation standards. Required Qualifications · Master's degree or higher in Physiology, Biomedical Sciences, Anatomy and Physiology, Medicine, Physician Associate Studies, or a closely related health sciences discipline. · Experience teaching medical physiology at the graduate and/or professional level is required. · Demonstrated expertise in human physiology and its clinical application. · Strong communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. · Commitment to excellence in graduate health professions education and student success. Preferred Qualifications · Terminal degree (PhD, MD, DO, DSc, DMSc, EdD, or equivalent) in a related discipline. · Experience teaching physiology within a Physician Associate, medical, nursing, or other graduate health professions program. · Experience integrating case-based instruction and active learning strategies into graduate-level courses. · Familiarity with curriculum assessment and continuous quality improvement processes in health professions education. About Alvernia University Alvernia University is a comprehensive Catholic university rooted in the Franciscan tradition, committed to academic excellence, ethical leadership, and service to others. The College of Health Sciences prepares future healthcare professionals through innovative education, experiential learning, interdisciplinary collaboration, and community engagement. The Physician Associate Program prepares compassionate, competent, and collaborative physician associates through a rigorous graduate curriculum that integrates foundational sciences, clinical medicine, patient care, and professional practice. Alvernia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from individuals committed to fostering excellence, inclusion, and belonging in higher education.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204519099128_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct-Part-time Medical Moral Theology Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nMedical Moral Theology (Healthcare Ethics) (Part-Time) -Instructor   Alvernia University invites applications as we have an immediate need for an Adjunct to teach Medical Moral Theology (Healthcare Ethics) in the fall semester. Position Responsibilities The course will run Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays from 1:25-2:15 from 8/24 through 12/11.  Prepare and deliver engaging, student-centered instruction. . Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Theology (or closely related field) Appointment This is a part-time adjunct faculty appointment. Teaching assignments are contingent upon enrollment and departmental needs.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204517565394_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Information Literacy Librarian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-21\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nJob Summary: Responsible for the planning, coordination, and supervision of the following major library activities: information literacy instruction and tools and research services.  Participates in library assessment planning and data collection.   With other professional staff, sets library-wide policies, determines library directions, and develops appropriate performance measures. Essential Functions: Promote Franciscan ideals and adherence to the Mission of the University as demonstrated by the University Ideal Characteristics.  As we are an equal opportunity employer committed to Franciscan values, all employees share responsibility for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in the performance of their roles while demonstrating service orientation, respect for all, intellectual curiosity, solution focus and innovation, and mutual accountability. Lead, present, and coordinate library information literacy instruction.  Work with faculty to provide information literacy sessions. Participate in library assessment activities including planning, measurement, and analysis of data.  Evaluates the effectiveness of library resources and services assessment and provides recommendations. Participate in digital and print collection development activities, and act as library liaison with the faculty in assigned academic areas. Lead reference staffing and tracking. Provide reference assistance to students, faculty, staff and community patrons.   Develop, update, and publish information literacy guides and other resources in all formats for the Franco Library. Additional Responsibilities: Train and manage a graduate assistant to populate and monitor all aspects of the library’s social media presence. Hire, train and supervise the library’s Graduate Assistants. Maintain library's webpage. Assist with technical services operations. Educate and assist faculty with Open Educational Resources (OER).  Engage with the university community through committee work, displays, service activities, etc.  Create and maintain library’s information literacy video collection.  Will be expected to work evening hours. Qualification/Education: Commitment to the mission statement, core values and goals of Alvernia University. A master’s degree in library science from an ALA-accredited institution. Academic library experience in reference services, information literacy instruction, and library assessment and data collection. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with staff; utilizes excellent communication and customer service skills.  Ability to adapt and lead in a changing library environment. Ability to work as part of a team as well as independently. Ability to effectively supervise student workers.    Physical Requirements: Attendance is required to perform the duties of this job.  Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Must be able to lift 15 pounds at times. Employee Benefits:   Join a team that values your well-being! We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support you and your family. Robust Health Coverage - Choose from three offered medical plans, plus dental and vision. Financial Security  - Enjoy university paid Life/AD&D insurance and Long-Term Disability, with options for Short-Term Disability and supplemental coverage for you and your family (including accident, critical illness, and hospital indemnity plans). Flexible spending accounts are also available. Exceptional Retirement - Start saving immediately with our 403(b) Retirement Plan . You will get 100% immediate vesting , a university gift contribution, and a generous match up to 5% of your deferrals. Time off & Flexibility - Take advantage of 20 paid holidays , including five floating holidays, and the possibility of flexible or hybrid work options for many roles. Invest in Your Future - Enjoy tuition remission benefits for yourself and your dependents. On-Campus Wellness  - Benefit-eligible employees on our main campus receive free access to our Medical & Counseling Center. Employee Meal Plan - This plan provides convenient, flexible dining options on campus at a reduced cost.",
