      "title": "Multiple Part-time (Adjunct) Accounting Instructors",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nAlvernia University Header School of Business is seeking applications for part-time (Adjunct) Instructors to teach the following Accounting undergraduate courses in the Fall 2026 semester, starting 8/24/2026 and ending 12/11/2026. BUS 301: Advanced Accounting , Tuesdays and Thursdays from 12:30 PM to 1:45 PM BUS 304: Federal Taxation , Tuesdays and Thursdays from 9:30 AM to 10:45 AM Please see the 2026-27 Undergraduate Catalog for course descriptions: https://catalog.alvernia.edu/ These courses are offered in class at the John R. Post Center at Reading CollegeTowne, 401 Penn Street, Reading, PA, 19601. Applicants must have a minimum of a master’s degree in accounting or a related field. Experience teaching accounting at the undergraduate level is preferred.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204407427569_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct-Assistant Track and Field Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-01\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nJob Summary: The Assistant Track & Field Coach is responsible for providing ethical leadership in assisting with all aspects of an NCAA Track & Field program, including, but not limited to, recruitment and retention of academically and athletically qualified student-athletes and preparing student-athletes for success through practice planning, strategy development, and skill instruction. Preference will be given to candidates with jumps, throws, and/or multi-event experience, but anyone interested in the position is encouraged to apply. Essential Functions: 1. Promote Franciscan ideals and adherence to the Mission of the University as demonstrated by the University Ideal Characteristics. As we are an equal opportunity employer committed to Franciscan values, all employees share responsibility for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in the performance of their roles while demonstrating service orientation, respect for all, intellectual curiosity, solution focus and innovation, and mutual accountability. 2. With the head coach, responsible for the design, implementation, and execution of a comprehensive recruiting strategy and plan that will identify, recruit, and retain academically and athletically qualified student-athletes in accordance with all university admissions standards and procedures; meet or exceed annual established recruiting goals. 3. With the head coach, responsible for the design, implementation, and execution of day-to-day practice coaching, meet-day coaching, and strength & conditioning for the applicable event group(s). 4. Attract, organize, and manage indoor track & field meets, including coordination with Event Management, setup, meet management, and breakdown. 5. Ensure commitment to the academic success of the student-athletes, including monitoring academic progress and attendance and involving appropriate academic support resources when necessary. 6. Foster a positive environment where student-athletes can learn, grow, and reach their potential; serve as a mentor, advisor, positive role model, and exemplar of good character and integrity; monitor discipline and conduct of student-athletes to foster personal growth and ensure adherence to community standards and appropriate codes of conduct/expectations. Additional Responsibilities: 1. With the head coach, maintain appropriate records and paperwork and ensure program (head coach, assistant coaches, student-athletes, etc.) compliance with all university, Middle Atlantic Conference (MAC), and NCAA policies, rules, and regulations. 2. Design and implement a formal communication plan that includes regular meetings with student-athletes. Seek volunteer service opportunities for student-athletes to aid in reaching personal, program, and departmental goals. 3. Assist the Head Track & Field Coach with planning, preparing, and implementing collegiate and high school competitions. 4. With the head coach, responsible for budget/purchasing planning to ensure a balanced budget annually. Qualifications/Education: 1. Commitment to the mission statement, core values, and goals of Alvernia University. 2. Bachelor’s degree and successful experience as a student-athlete and/or coach is required. College coaching experience is preferred. 3. A demonstrated ability to effectively communicate with student-athletes, coaches, athletic trainers, and athletic administration. Commitment to be a good colleague and team player. 4. Demonstrated problem-solving, strong leadership, communication, organizational, and team-building skills/capabilities; ability to handle and prioritize multiple tasks/projects in a fast-paced environment. 5. Commitment to fostering a positive student-athlete experience where the safety, health, and well-being of student-athletes is paramount. Physical Requirements: 1. Attendance is required in order to perform the duties of this job. 2. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends. 3. Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer. 4. Must be able to lift 15 pounds at times. 5. Frequent travel is required.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204333588534_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Alumni and Constituent Engagement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-16\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nJob Summary The Alumni and Constituent Engagement Coordinator supports the implementation of engagement strategies that strengthen relationships among alumni, students, parents, and community members. The position manages alumni marketing and communications initiatives, supports the operational and logistical coordination of key engagement programs and events, and assists with initiatives related to the Alvernia Women’s Council (AWC). The role works collaboratively across campus to enhance constituent participation, visibility, and affinity for Alvernia University. Essential Functions Promote Franciscan ideals and model the University Mission by demonstrating the Ideal Characteristics: service-oriented, respectful, inclusive, intellectually curious, innovative, accountable, and committed to problem-solving. Develop and implement marketing and communications strategies that promote alumni and constituent engagement opportunities across print, digital, email, social media, web, and emerging communication platforms. Create and manage content calendars for alumni and constituent engagement communications.  Develop promotional materials, event communications, newsletters, social media content, and digital storytelling initiatives highlighting alumni, students, and community impact. Maintain and update alumni and engagement-related webpages and digital communication platforms. Assist in coordinating operational logistics and event execution for major engagement programs and signature events with the Director of Alumni and Constituent Engagement. Assist with post-event stewardship, evaluations, reporting, and follow-up communications to support ongoing engagement and continuous improvement efforts. Support the Alvernia Women’s Council (AWC) through event coordination, communications, volunteer support, meeting logistics, sponsorship support, and program promotion. Support alumni and constituent engagement initiatives designed to strengthen lifelong connections with students and alumni through mentoring, networking, volunteerism, and career engagement opportunities. Collaborate with campus partners, including Athletics, Student Affairs, Academic Affairs, Career Development, Enrollment Management, and Marketing and Communications, to support engagement initiatives and institutional priorities. Utilize Raiser’s Edge NXT (RENXT) to track engagement activity, event participation, volunteer involvement, communication efforts, and constituent interactions while maintaining accurate records and reporting. Represent the University at engagement events and programs both on campus and regionally as needed. Qualification/Education: Commitment to the mission statement, core values, and goals of Alvernia University. Baccalaureate Degree required  Strategic thinker with excellent organizational skills and the ability to manage several projects simultaneously. Must be innovative, self-motivated, creative, flexible, dedicated, and able to work both independently and as an active member of a team  High-level proficiency in utilizing all social media platforms as well as the Microsoft Office Suite.  Availability to work some nights and weekends in order to attend events and meet with alumni, including travel that may require overnight stays.  Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects under deadline pressure.  Ability to work collaboratively with various University constituents, volunteers, and campus partners.  Physical Requirements: Attendance is required in order to perform the duties of this job.  Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Travel required Must be able to lift 15 pounds at times. Employee Benefits: Join a team that values your well-being! We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support you and your family: Robust Health Coverage:  Choose from three offered medical plans, plus dental and vision. Financial Security:  Enjoy University-paid life/AD&D insurance and long-term disability, with options for short-term disability and supplemental coverage for you and your family (including accident, critical illness, and hospital indemnity plans). Flexible spending accounts are also available. Exceptional Retirement:  Start saving immediately with our 403(b) Retirement Plan . You will get 100% immediate vesting , a University gift contribution, and a generous match up to 5% of your deferrals. Time Off & Flexibility:  Take advantage of 20 paid holidays, including 5 floating holidays, each year, and the possibility of flexible or hybrid work options for many roles. Invest in Your Future:  Enjoy tuition remission benefits for yourself and your dependents. On-Campus Wellness:  Benefit-eligible employees on our main campus receive free access to our Medical & Counseling Center. Employee Meal Plan : This plan provides convenient, flexible dining options on campus at a reduced cost.",
      "department": ""
    },
