    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204093333941_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Department of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-27\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nJOB SUMMARY: Under the direction of the Chair, the GA will support: 1. administrative and organizational tasks associated with the program’s service learning experiences, including activities at and for the pro bono center, 2. administrative and organizational tasks associated with the clinical education program, under the direction of the Director of Clinical Education, 3. administrative and organizational tasks as directed by the department’s administrative assistant, which may include assignments related to record keeping, department correspondence, student/faculty organizations, etc. The position handles a varied work schedule and the ability to prioritize work duties as they deem necessary and under the supervision of the PT Department Chair.    ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Assist the PT Department Chair, Program Director, Director of Clinical Education, PT faculty, and PT Administrative Assistant in the completion of daily tasks, as deemed appropriate. Assist the PT Department Chair, Program Director, Director of Clinical Education, PT faculty, and PT Administrative Assistant with special projects and assignments. Compose correspondence, answer inquiries, set up appointments, organize and schedule meetings, order office and lab supplies, etc. Provide support to PT faculty and adjunct faculty with the administrative aspects of teaching that do not relate to student grading, advising, and assessment of learning. These tasksinclude, but are not limited to: obtaining desk copies, photocopying, archiving course materials, and organizational management. Assist faculty in the instruction of laboratory sessions. Assistwith department events and projects, including but not limited to university and community events, etc. Provide support to the Director of Clinical Education(DCE)for a variety of tasks associated with the clinical education program including communication and correspondence with clinical sites, obtaining and maintaining clearances, record keeping and organization of clinical education documents, etc. as directed and supervised by the DCE. Support and maintain the physical space and supports faculty and student leadership in overall management of the pro bono center and service-learning activities at a variety of settings.  Handle the day-to-day activities according to the PT Department Chair and Program Director’s general instructions and notify the Chair and Director of upcoming events and timelines. Promote Franciscan ideals and adherence to the Mission of the Department and University. QUALIFICATIONS/EDUCATION: Commitment to the mission statement, core values and goals of the PT Department and Alvernia University. 2.   Earned bachelor's degree and currently enrolled as a full-time student within the DPT Program. 4.   Strong organizational and communication (written and oral) skills. 5.   Strong PC skills and experience including: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Microsoft Teams. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: 1.  Attendance is required in order to perform the duties of this job.  2.  Ability to sit for long periods of time while working on the computer.  3.  Ability to coordinate multiple activities and projects and prioritize own work. 4.  Ability to stay focused on job at hand with constant interruptions.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9203334619924_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Gross Anatomy",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-10-30\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nJob Summary: The College of Health Sciences at Alvernia University is seeking an adjunct, gross anatomy instructor to contribute to the Master of Medical Science – Physician Associate program. The successful candidate will primarily facilitate large group lectures and small group lab sessions of gross anatomy in the first-year curriculum of the professional phase of the Physician Associate program. Essential Functions: · Teaching in the Physician Associate Program; · Contribute to the planning, development, and evaluation of anatomy lecture and laboratory sessions within the Physician Associate Program, ensuring the curriculum aligns with the learning outcomes of the program; · Promote adequate standards of linguistic expression in writing and speech; · Carry out lectures, labs and responsibilities effectively; · Prepare examination questions as well as grades for a course or portion of a course; · Meet classes according to published schedule; · Commit to working in a multicultural environment that fosters diversity; · Promote Franciscan ideals and adherence to the Mission of the University as demonstrated by the University Ideal Characteristics. As we are an equal opportunity employer committed to Franciscan values, all employees share responsibility for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in the performance of their roles while demonstrating service orientation, respect for all, intellectual curiosity, solution focus and innovation, and mutual accountability. Supervision: · Received: Physician Associate Program Director · Given: N/A Required Qualifications: · Master's Degree or higher in related field · Minimum of 3 years of work experience in the field of anatomy · Minimum of 3 years of teaching experience at the college/university level · Commitment to graduate and professional education and student success · Excellent organizational and communication skills · Must be able to work independently and effectively interact with a wide array of parties at all levels (students, faculty, and administration/staff Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching gross anatomy /functional with Anatomage-based labs. Physical Requirements: · Physical attendance · Lifting up to 15 pounds at times",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=1b9ea04c-142e-4aa7-8d21-45439ca5b76b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201255012728_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Engineering Management Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-08-08\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nEngineering Management Adjunct Faculty Pool | John R. Post School of Engineering | Remote The John R. Post School of Engineering at Alvernia University invites applications to its adjunct faculty pool in Engineering Management. Courses are remote and largely asynchronous. Experienced engineering leaders, project managers, operations and manufacturing professionals, and other technical professionals are encouraged to apply, including those new to college teaching. Applicants should apply to the pool even when there is no immediate course need; qualified applicants may be considered for future semesters as needs arise. Candidates hired into the pool are contracted separately for individual courses as assignments become available. Pool membership does not guarantee a course assignment. Candidates should be comfortable creating engaging, accessible online learning experiences for working professionals and graduate students. Potential teaching areas Project and Operations Management Engineering project management, production and operations management, and applied management of engineering and technical organizations. Analytics, Risk, and Process Improvement Data-driven decision-making, risk analysis, process improvement, applied analytics, Lean, and Six Sigma. Leadership and Strategy Strategic team leadership, organizational effectiveness, and leadership of technical teams and engineering organizations. Digital Engineering and Smart Manufacturing Artificial intelligence, informatics, cybersecurity, additive manufacturing, smart manufacturing, robotics, Internet of Things, simulation, and digital twins. Experience teaching or leading professionals in online, graduate, or continuing-education settings is especially valued. Preferred qualifications We particularly welcome experienced engineering and technical professionals who can bring current workplace practice into the online classroom. Prior college teaching is not required. Preferred candidates will have at least a master's degree in Engineering Management, Industrial Engineering, Systems Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering or a closely related field and approximately five or more years of relevant professional experience. These are preferred qualifications, not absolute minimums; comparable combinations of advanced education, professional licensure, specialized expertise, leadership, industry experience, and teaching will be considered. Completion of the Fundamentals of Engineering (FE) exam, Engineer in Training (EIT) certification, and/or Professional Engineer (PE) licensure is a plus. Experience with online teaching, graduate education, professional education, or workforce training is also valued. Application and employment requirements How to apply All applications and application materials must be submitted through Alvernia University's ADP employment portal for the specific adjunct pool posting. Submit a current resume or curriculum vitae and a brief letter of interest identifying the courses or subject areas you believe you are qualified to teach. Do not email application materials. Email inquiries are welcome, but a formal application through ADP is required for consideration. Work authorization Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and able to accept employment with Alvernia University without current or future employer sponsorship. Questions and inquiries Prospective applicants may contact Dr. Joseph M. Mahoney, Chair of the John R. Post School of Engineering, at joseph.mahoney@alvernia.edu with questions about the School, the adjunct pool, or potential teaching needs. Application materials must be submitted through ADP and should not be emailed. Equal employment opportunity Alvernia University is an equal-opportunity employer committed to Franciscan values. People of all faith backgrounds, as well as people with no faith affiliation, are welcome and encouraged to apply. All employees share responsibility for advancing a culture of care in the performance of their roles while demonstrating service orientation, respect for all, intellectual curiosity, solution focus and innovation, and mutual accountability. Alvernia University strives to be a community supportive of diverse perspectives and identities.",
      "department": ""
    },
