      "title": "Faculty Adjunct, Neuroscience for Rehabilitation",
      "description": "Posted: 2024-06-27\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nADJUNCT, NEUROSCIENCE FOR REHABILITATION Job Highlights Required qualifications include a minimum of a Master's Degree in Athletic Training, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, or related fields. Preference will be given to candidates who have previous teaching experience. Complete applications are to include a cover letter, CV, and contact information for three professional references, and background clearances. Responsibilities Adjunct faculty are expected to teach, prepare course materials, be available to meet with students outside of regularly scheduled class time, and provide support and guidance for students. Job description Alvernia University is currently seeking highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach the Neuroscience for Rehabilitation at our Reading campus in fall, 2024. This course examines structure and functioning of the human nervous system through an integrated analysis of neuroanatomy, neurophysiology and neurochemistry. This course emphasizes clinically relevant neuroscience concepts, focusing on application to patient rehabilitation and therapeutic approaches.",
