      "title": "Part Time Bus Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2021-12-15\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPosition Title:  Transportation Shuttle Driver ( evenings and weekends are required)   Job Summary: Responsible for the safe operation of the University Shuttles for the Transportation department of Alvernia University.  Essential Functions: Promote Franciscan ideals and adherence to the Mission of the University as demonstrated by the University Ideal Characteristics.  As we are an equal opportunity employer committed to Franciscan values, all employees share responsibility for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in the performance of their roles while demonstrating: service orientation, respect for all, intellectual curiosity, solution focus and innovation, and mutual accountability. Provide transportation services for Alvernia University Record statistical ridership Provide daily inspection, report, and maintain fuel level and cleanliness of vehicles Be friendly and courteous towards customers Obey all governmental laws and guidelines pertaining to safe transport Be punctual and stringent on timings and make no delays in transportation Qualifications/Education: Commitment to the mission statement, core values and goals of Alvernia University Good organizational skills High School Diploma CDL certification with air brake endorsement Medical certifications as deemed necessary for CDL endorsement Additional Comments, Tasks and Responsibilities: Assist in repairs and maintenance on equipment and vehicles Perform checks to ensure safety Responsible for filing reports on equipment, delays, incident or accident occurrences Keep communication open with drivers and staff Occasionally assist in some additional Utility functions  Physical Requirements: Attendance is required in order to perform the duties of this job.  Health and wellness certifications as required by law and policy to provide transportation services. Capable of lifting up to 50 lbs.",
      "department": ""
    },
